<Project>

  <!--
    THE single source of truth for the app's version. Nothing else in the repo may hardcode a
    version number: the csproj, the APK filename, the build manifest and the tests all derive from
    the four properties below (derivation lives in Directory.Build.props).

    Edit this file with `pwsh scripts/bump-version.ps1 -Patch` (or -Minor / -Major / -Set 2.1.0)
    rather than by hand, so the build number is reset with the same commit.

      FdVersionMajor.FdVersionMinor.FdVersionPatch  - the semantic version an artist would quote.
      FdBuildNumber                                 - re-releases of the same semantic version
                                                      (a rebuild that fixes packaging, not code).

    FdBuildNumber is written by scripts/build-apk.ps1, which consumes the next one on every build
    and commits it here after the publish succeeds. Expect it to move without you editing it; a
    semantic bump resets it to 0.

    Ranges are enforced by VersionTests: minor, patch and build are each 0-99, because all four
    numbers are packed into one Android versionCode:

      versionCode = major*1000000 + minor*10000 + patch*100 + build

    versionCode must increase on every APK a device is asked to upgrade to, and Android/Play will
    never accept a lower one for the same ApplicationId. The packing keeps it monotonic in the
    semantic version for free (1.2.3+0 is 1020300, 1.2.4+0 is 1020400) and leaves room for major
    up to 2147 before the int32 ceiling.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <FdVersionMajor>0</FdVersionMajor>
    <FdVersionMinor>2</FdVersionMinor>
    <FdVersionPatch>0</FdVersionPatch>
    <FdBuildNumber>1</FdBuildNumber>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
